Hello. I've submitted an Averatec 3250HX-01 DSDT and I would like to be 
able to customize it then load it into the kernel without having to 
recompile the kernel. The Averatec 3225 DSDT looks as if it is for the 
same board; that DSDT shows me the temperature of the CPU and changes 
fan behavior (doesn't seem to take advantage of less-than-full fan 
speeds) but causes excessive interrupts on irq 11 and everything in 
/proc/acpi/ takes longer.

How do I get started? Is there some way to twiddle with the relevant 
pm/control bits without having to edit the DSDT and reboot?

